		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Satellite operation]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3284&amp;p=26256#p26256"><![CDATA[
AMSAT (<a href="https://amsat.org" class="postlink">https://amsat.org</a>) is the amateur radio organization which helps get satellites built, coordinated, and launched. Please support them!<br><br>AMSAT operational status of all satellites: <a href="https://amsat.org/status/" class="postlink">https://amsat.org/status/</a><br>Note: This is crowdsourced so it can be wrong. Submit your contact at bottom of page.<br><br>The TEVELs and PO-101 operate on a schedule: <a href="https://df2et.de/tevel/" class="postlink">https://df2et.de/tevel/</a><br>Note: TEVEL-1 and TEVEL-8 were confirmed dead at launch by the owner.<br><br>ISS dedicated status page: <a href="https://ariss.org/current-status-of-iss-stations.html" class="postlink">https://ariss.org/current-status-of-iss-stations.html</a><br>ISS is the only current satellite that supports packet radio / APRS.<br><br>Maya 5 and Maya 6 are not operational yet, so are not included in satellites.txt in the CPS.<br><br>UVSQ-SAT has only been operational a couple of days a year so it’s not included in satellites.txt in the CPS.<br><br>AO-92 is dead because of failed batteries.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Sep 15, 2023 11:17 am</p><hr />
